//! # keel-ffi
//!
//! The bindings ([ADR-0025](../../../../docs/adr/0025-bindings.md)): the device runtime as a
//! [`Register`] object the platform shells drive, its views as records and its refusals as
//! [`KeelError`], generated by `UniFFI`. Kotlin, from the compiled library, by the crate's
//! `uniffi-bindgen` (with the `bindgen` feature).
//!
//! The one place in the kernel that reads the system's clock and the operating system's
//! randomness, for the register. Like the runtime it holds, this crate isn't built for `wasm32`.

uniffi::setup_scaffolding!();

mod error;
mod records;
mod register;

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests;

pub use error::KeelError;
pub use records::*;
pub use register::{Register, demo_profile, new_device, print_tcp};
